      {
        "id": 105861,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-07T11:37:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, the villain character card is <span class=\"bbcode-i\">always</span> going to be the first card in play in the game, thus you follow its instructions before any other card which has an effect during the various phases of the villain turn. So, Voss's turn begins. Say you killed his last Minion during the last round, so now he has none, so you look at his card and see that he flips. Then it's his Play phase. He plays Forced Deployment. Assuming he has no other cards out, you come to his End phase, in which he hits the highest and lowest hero targets (because he is flipped). Now you have a round in which to destroy Forced Deployment if you wish, so all the Minions will come out then and you have the remainder of the round to kill them. If you don't destroy Forced Deployment early, it comes around to Voss's turn again and you check his character card's Start phase actions. Check number of Minions in play - still zero, so he doesn't flip back just yet. Then you check Forced Deployment, which has the Start phase action of destroying itself. It does so, and thus brings all the Minions back out of the trash. That is the end of Voss's Start phase, as no other card currently in play will act at this point (unless Ab'Zero has Sub-Zero Atmosphere out, in which case all the Minions will deal their damage now…and actually Voss would also have done right before you moved onto Forced Deployment). then he plays a card, and then he and his Minions deal their damage. If there are still two or more Minions in play at the start of his <span class=\"bbcode-i\">next</span> turn, it says in his Start phase that he flips back under these conditions, so <span class=\"bbcode-i\">that</span> is when he flips back to his front side.</p>\n<p>If you <span class=\"bbcode-i\">had</span> destroyed Forced Deployment before Voss's turn came round, but didn't kill enough Minions for there to be fewer than two in play, he would instead flip back on his next turn.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:36.395Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
