      {
        "id": 105862,
        "name": "LevelUpLeo",
        "username": "LevelUpLeo",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/{size}/2394_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-07T15:33:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That pretty much answers my question, but the scenario I came across was that Voss was flipped the same turn Forced Deployment came out (which sucked). Voss still had 2 minions out when&nbsp;<span>Forced Deployment was played. As the turn came around, the 2 minions were KO'd (environment, I'm sure). Turn started, so I flipped Voss since he had no minions. Forced Deployment then gets destroyed and so all the minions from the trash (like... 5 or something that game) come out. I assumed that Voss wouldn't get flipped back, despite the fact that it is still the \"start of the villain phase\" and he now has more than 1 minion. Just wanted to make sure.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>(And yeah, that end of villain turn sucked.)</span></p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:35:36.471Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
